============================================================
 SC LAB M1-L2: DENY BY DEFAULT FIREWALL
 Pod: {{ pod_name }} ({{ prefix }})
 Gateway: http://{{ gw_ip }}
============================================================

SCENARIO:
The {{ pod_name }}-GW firewall currently has an "Allow Any Any"
rule that permits ALL traffic through the firewall. This is
a critical security misconfiguration.

YOUR TASK:
1. Log into the pfSense web UI at http://{{ gw_ip }}
   Credentials: admin / pfsense

2. Navigate to Firewall > Rules > LAN

3. OBSERVE the current rules:
   - You will see an "Allow ALL traffic" rule
   - This means ANY device can reach ANY destination
   - This violates CMMC SC.L1-3.13.1

4. RECONFIGURE to Deny-By-Default:
   a. DELETE the "Allow Any Any" rule
   b. CREATE specific rules that ONLY allow:
      - DNS to DC01 (10.50.1.10 port 53)
      - Web traffic (ports 80, 443)
      - ICMP/Ping for troubleshooting
   c. Verify the DEFAULT DENY rule is at the bottom

5. VERIFY:
   - Business applications still work (DNS, web)
   - Unauthorized traffic is blocked
   - Check Firewall > Logs to see blocked traffic

SUCCESS CRITERIA:
  [ ] No "Allow Any Any" rule exists
  [ ] Only necessary traffic is permitted
  [ ] Default deny is the last rule
  [ ] DNS resolution works
  [ ] Web browsing works

Save evidence: Screenshot your final rule set and save to:
